<div class="qul-docs">
  <h2>About word by word translation</h2>

  <p>
    A word by word translation gives the meaning of each individual word of the Quran rather than of the
    ayah as a whole. It is what powers word-level tooltips and learner views. The data is available as
    <strong>JSON</strong> and <strong>SQLite</strong>.
  </p>

  <div class="docs-callout docs-callout-info">
    Words are identified by <strong>location</strong> — <code>surah:ayah:word</code>. So
    <code>2:3:5</code> is the fifth word of Surah Al-Baqarah, ayah 3. Word numbering starts at 1.
  </div>

  <h2>JSON</h2>
  <p>A flat object keyed by word location.</p>
  <div class="docs-code">
    <div class="docs-code-header"><span>JSON</span></div>
    <pre><code>{
  "1:1:1": "In (the) name",
  "1:1:2": "(of) Allah",
  "1:1:3": "the Most Gracious",
  "1:1:4": "the Most Merciful"
}</code></pre>
  </div>

  <h2>SQLite columns</h2>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Column</th>
        <th>Type</th>
        <th>What it holds</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><code>surah_number</code></td>
        <td>INTEGER</td>
        <td>Surah the word belongs to.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>ayah_number</code></td>
        <td>INTEGER</td>
        <td>Ayah within that surah.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>word_number</code></td>
        <td>TEXT</td>
        <td>Position of the word within the ayah, starting at 1.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>text</code></td>
        <td>TEXT</td>
        <td>The translation of that word.</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <div class="docs-callout docs-callout-warning">
    This resource carries the translations only, not the Arabic. To show the word itself alongside its
    meaning you also need a word by word Quran script from the
    <a href="/resources/quran-script">Quran Scripts</a> page — join the two on the word location.
  </div>
</div>
    
